-- Topic and knowledge points

-- Lesson T1: city trees

B. Choosing the right species matters. A tree with a wide crown gives more shade, but its roots may damage pavements if there is not enough soil. Planners therefore leave a larger pit of soil around each young tree.

C. Young trees also need water for their first three summers. In one fictional town, volunteers "adopt" a tree near their home and water it once a week.', 'VALID');
