-- Lesson T2: forests and seasons

B. As the days become shorter, the tree stops producing chlorophyll. Yellow and orange colours, which were in the leaf all summer, finally become visible.

C. Red colours are different: they are made in autumn itself, mostly when the days are sunny and the nights are cool. This is why some years are more colourful than others.', 'VALID');
